Performance: Nino writes arrays and lists of raw values and fixed-size types straight into a `PipeWriter`, `ArrayBufferWriter<byte>` or any other `IBufferWriter<byte>` through one `GetSpan` of their size, instead of copying them from its scratch buffer (also `ArraySegment<T>`, array-backed `Memory<T>` and single-segment `ReadOnlySequence<T>` of raw values on .NET Standard 2.1 and later, and their multidimensional arrays on .NET 8 and later).
